If I understand correctly, the pthread_attr_t instance must live all long the thread extend.

So the following code is bad:

```C
int x_thread_create(
			x_thread_t *tid,
                        x_thread_cb entry,
			void *arg,
			int detached)
{
        int rc;
	pthread_attr_t attr;

	pthread_attr_init(&attr);
	if (detached)
		pthread_attr_setdetachstate(&attr, PTHREAD_CREATE_DETACHED);
	rc = pthread_create(tid, &attr, (void*(*)(void*))entry, arg) ? -errno : 0;
	pthread_attr_destroy(&attr);
       return rc;
}
```

I reached it because logs are telling `<err> os: tid 0x20001418 is in use!`
And IMHO it leads to memory leak because when the thread stops, k_thread_stack_free isn't called.

Can you confirm my analysis please?

